-- title:
--   Ivanov’s 278-state table and the four state identifications
-- statement:
--   Let U₂ be the 278-state machine whose complete instruction table is given in Ivanov's thesis, appendix printed pages 128–129. Its initial state is 1 and its unique halt state is 278. Let π identify precisely the triples (45,150,270), (46,151,271), (200,230,256), and (201,231,257), leaving all other states distinct. Representatives are the first member of each triple. The quotient instruction at a representative is
--
--   $$U(\pi(q))=\pi_*\bigl(U_2(\pi(q))\bigr),$$
--
--   where π acts on destinations and preserves counter operations and branch order. Consistency with every member of each class is a separate theorem, rather than an assumed property of this definition.
--
--   The entire table has been transcribed from the cited thesis and compared entry by entry with the companion transcription. The counters and state transitions are concrete data; no universality premise is part of the definition.
-- source:
--   Thanin Quartz, Ivan O. Shevchenko, Hans De Sterck, Jun Liu, STOC 2027 submission #1062 (October 2026), §4.1 and Appendix B.1, PDF p. 15 / printed p. 13; supporting data: Sergiu Ivanov, PhD thesis (2015), §5.2 and appendix printed pp.128–129 (PDF pp.146–147), https://www.ibisc.univ-evry.fr/~sivanov/content/phd/ivanov-phd.pdf

import Mathlib
